{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/116378-questions-on-no-seeming-and-order-of-oneirophysics","id":116378,"title":"Questions on No Seeming and Order of Oneirophysics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-19T23:59:38-07:00","id":116378,"title":"Questions on No Seeming and Order of Oneirophysics","content":"1) Just an idle question unrelated to any character, why is No Seeming a 2 point Merit. It seems that while it does have no downside (Unlike the Seemings, which do) and has a fully human appearance, the one real advantage you get is not really better than having a Seeming, even with the curse, especially given No Seeming characters cannot have a Kith, which tends to be another source of abilities. Plus they get fewer Contracts favored. It seems odd that is something you have to pay points for. Any thoughts?<br /> <br /> 2) We've had a couple players eyeballing the Order of Oneirophysics and the flaw seems needlessly harsh...especially given they seem to be the only Entitlement in the game that gives a flaw (unless you count the penalty for Vizieral Council when leaving, which is not exactly an apples to apples comparison). While the Order does get some nice stuff, it does not seem out of line with some of the other entitlements that get similarly nice stuff with no downside, and the OoO is not exactly the best. I've been considering reducing or removing the penalty to bring it in line with other Entitlements...does anyone else have any thoughts?<br /> <br /> ETA: For clarity, since it was asked below, I am talking about the -1 to -3 to Presence rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-20-2014, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T00:30:20-07:00","id":116396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/116378-questions-on-no-seeming-and-order-of-oneirophysics#post116378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems odd that is something you have to pay points for. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see lowering it to a 1 dot Merit, but I think it does have value. The bonus to Clarity rolls is a big deal (at least until we see a revamped Clarity system GMC style) considering how easily changelings can be put into situations that require a roll. Not having a Curse is also nice. The XP lost in favored Contracts is slim considering the sheer number of Contracts out there anyway. It only really hurts if you want to pick up multiple Seeming Contracts from the same Seeming. Likewise you don't get a Kith, but there's lots of ways to replicate most Kith Blessings with other Merits. So you aren't permanently locked out of most of those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We've had a couple players eyeballing the Order of Oneirophysics and the flaw seems needlessly harsh... </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by &quot;flaw?&quot; Are you talking about the drawback of their top tier power?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T00:52:37-07:00","id":116405,"title":"","content":"I mean the -1 to -3 penalty on all Presence rolls depending on Rank. Apologies, I should have been clearer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T01:22:55-07:00","id":116413,"title":"","content":"No Seemings Definitely get an advantage. My character is going to get high Wyrd (A feat now currently possible within a smaller time period due to GMC rules) and while a few of the other people in the group are also advancing as much as I am. They are kind of dreading it for the high penalties but eh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T04:38:47-07:00","id":116442,"title":"","content":"I dunno about that. My party has an Elemental Earthbones/Gargantuan Dual Kith, and the benefits for increasing Wyrd are absurd. After about a year of our current campaign, he hit Wyrd 6. His Seeming and Kith benefit produce +12 health when he needs it. Every level of Wyrd adds another +2 to that possible bonus, and at his next level of Wyrd his Kith evolves and he gains the Gargantuan benefit of adding half Wyrd to Strength rolls. Just on its own, +7 health for a point of Glamour and 4 extra dice on a Brawl attack is a pretty nice bonus that happily cancels the Curse for that level. The Elemental Curses aren't that much fun, but that ever-climbing health buff (and the promise of +5 permanent health should he ever get to Wyrd 10) is more than enough to keep him pushing on for the top.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I don't think No Seeming has a cost because it confers an advantage. I think it has a cost more to demonstrate how rare it is. It has a bit of a perk, so it isn't a complete waste of points, and a bonus to Clarity rolls is quite useful. That said, it's not something that would generally be considered a &quot;competitive&quot; choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T05:26:56-07:00","id":116451,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it's better to be a No Seeming fae than a wisened or Fairest changeling at Wyrd 10. Especially fairest who get the rawest deal of the bunch. That bonus clarity is really good. The real fun comes from the story telling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T06:10:38-07:00","id":116467,"title":"","content":"Of course. Like I said, No Seeming seems to have been costed with its scarcity in mind. You pay experience for some different roleplaying opportunities. Not better or worse ones than playing any other Seeming/Kith of course, but rather ones that don't come up as often.<br /> <br /> Beasts don't have as bad a curse as the Seemings you listed, but their Seeming Evolutions are laughably bad as well (mostly new Animal Ken specialties...). That said, I do believe the No Seeming Changeling will nearly always be at a disadvantage (although they certainly win over Fairest at high Wyrd when it comes to being trapped in a room with a Fae for long periods). It's just the price you pay for those unique roleplay options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T06:15:38-07:00","id":116468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/116378-questions-on-no-seeming-and-order-of-oneirophysics?p=116467#post116467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. Like I said, No Seeming seems to have been costed with its scarcity in mind. You pay experience for some different roleplaying opportunities. Not better or worse ones than playing any other Seeming/Kith of course, but rather ones that don't come up as often.<br /> <br /> Beasts don't have as bad a curse as the Seemings you listed, but their Seeming Evolutions are laughably bad as well (mostly new Animal Ken specialties...). That said, I do believe the No Seeming Changeling will nearly always be at a disadvantage (although they certainly win over Fairest at high Wyrd when it comes to being trapped in a room with a Fae for long periods). It's just the price you pay for those unique roleplay options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wized can no longer use xp on like 2/3rs of their stats. Darklings weren't so great either. I think only elementals really get a better deal than the rest of them. The disadvantages are pretty high all around though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T11:34:53-07:00","id":116604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/116378-questions-on-no-seeming-and-order-of-oneirophysics?p=116442#post116442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno about that. My party has an Elemental Earthbones/Gargantuan Dual Kith, and the benefits for increasing Wyrd are absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's a fair example. Most of the Kiths do not provide Wyrd scaling bonuses. I think this touches on a much bigger issue of the completely huge variety of powerlevels of the Kiths.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you take a Runnerswift/Hunterheart, a No Seeming character could just buy Lethal Mien and Fleet of Foot. Both at start would leave the No Seeming character at... costing 1 more Merit dot.<br /> <br /> The large variations in Kith potency and how easy a Kith bonus can be reproduced with other means makes it really hard to say how competitive a No Seeming character will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T11:56:48-07:00","id":116617,"title":"","content":"No Seeming does give you a bonus to resist degeneration, which is kind of a big deal. More importantly, though, it's one of the 'partial transformation' merits, for representing people that have started to become changelings, but haven't completed the process - it'd be a rare chronicle where players get those. If you look at it as a merit for mortals (though that's technically incorrect), it represents having changed enough to have a dot of Wyrd, carry/harvest Glamour, gain Contracts, and make Pledges - but not enough to have taken an inhuman form, or start losing their connection to reality. It'd be an interesting character at Wryd 10... they'd be a pretty classic Sidhe, I think (of the Magic Peoples of the Mounds variety, not the 'most Fair').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T12:33:57-07:00","id":116635,"title":"","content":"High Wyrd effects are optional, and only going to apply to a minority of games, though. Now, it is not irrelevant to the discussion, as it will likely apply to mine, but you have to remember most Changeling games don't hit Wyrd 6 even. So we are talking about something that does not come up much, and you still get frailties and the need for glamour to survive regardless. I am unsure that not getting a more severe weakness in ~20% of games but also not getting greatly enhanced powers in those games justifies the cost. My other game only had people at 7 (though a couple elected to not go past 5) and the weaknesses did not bug them so much. Honestly the frailties became more relevant.<br /> <br /> The point about Kiths is not untrue, though you could buy those same merits and do it better by possessing those things and doing it the same way. Plus some Kiths are reproducible with Merits, others not. I will say the reason many Kiths don't have bonuses is they are not in the main book. They would have bonuses, just they don't have official rules for them (note to self, high Wyrd bonuses for the Kiths in Winter Masques, Swords at Dawn, Victorian Lost and Grim Fears may make for a good thread, if that road is not trodden). Still that raises a good point....you can get some of those effects without a kith.<br /> <br /> One thing people seem to like with Changeling (and miss in other games) is the 9 agains and glamour buying dice though, both of which will be barred a character who has No Seeming. Of course, not all players like the same things.<br /> <br /> I'd like some talk on OoO too...No Seeming is sort of idle speculation for me since none of my players took it or are terribly interested, but I will need to make a ruling on that weakness for that entitlement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T17:21:05-07:00","id":116751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/116378-questions-on-no-seeming-and-order-of-oneirophysics?p=116604#post116604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that's a fair example. Most of the Kiths do not provide Wyrd scaling bonuses. I think this touches on a much bigger issue of the completely huge variety of powerlevels of the Kiths.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you take a Runnerswift/Hunterheart, a No Seeming character could just buy Lethal Mien and Fleet of Foot. Both at start would leave the No Seeming character at... costing 1 more Merit dot.<br /> <br /> The large variations in Kith potency and how easy a Kith bonus can be reproduced with other means makes it really hard to say how competitive a No Seeming character will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm running off memory here, but isn't Lethal Mien a 3 dot merit? It also has a Wyrd prerequisite of 3, so there's no way a starting character could ever have it (especially if they also need to spend 2 dots on No Seeming). Even in this scenario, where the effects can be replicated by merits, the normal Changeling effectively has a &quot;free&quot; merit from their Kith. They are also eligible to buy the very same merits that the No Seeming Changeling can buy, getting a better bonus for a lower cost (since they don't need to buy the No Seeming merit). That Hunterheart/Runnerswift you describe spends the same on the Dual Kith Merit that the No Seeming Changeling spends on the No Seeming Merit. Then they can both, for the same price, buy Lethal Mien and Fleet of Foot. The difference is that the Beast in this scenario has +4 Speed and +2 lethal weapons, where the No Seeming Changeling is +2 and +1. Same amount of experience spent on each, and the only downside is that the Beast suffers a -4 Unskilled penalty on Mental Skills and no 10 again when using Intelligence. We'll assume the various Beast blessings roughly equate to the +1 on Clarity checks. The Beast is well ahead in that scenario, I feel.<br /> <br /> Anywho, on the matter of the Order of Oneirophysics, I've just re-read the entry and I can't see the -1 to -3 penalty to Presence rolls you were talking about. Which section is it under?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T22:10:49-07:00","id":116826,"title":"","content":"The Mien Section, it is kinda hidden.<br /> <br /> You can start with 3 Wyrd, just not 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T17:05:18-07:00","id":117249,"title":"","content":"I know you can start with 3 Wyrd. You can't start with 3 Wyrd, buy a 2 dot Merit for No Seeming, and then buy a 3 dot Merit for Lethal Mien to replicate the Hunterheart Kith, all at character creation.<br /> <br /> And... huh, I've read through the Oneirophysics entry three times in preparation for using them in my game. Never once picked up on that. Personally, I think I'm planning on just ignoring it. Entitlement benefits are rarely all that impressive on their own, they don't need a handicap thrown in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T20:16:19-07:00","id":117351,"title":"","content":"Nah not with basic starting stats, no. You are correct.<br /> <br /> Only reason I caught that (the Presence penalty) was someone was looking to play it and pointed it out. I'd have noticed it re-reading for them to play the Entitlement, but not on a casual read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T20:24:59-07:00","id":117354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/116378-questions-on-no-seeming-and-order-of-oneirophysics?p=117249#post117249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you can start with 3 Wyrd. You can't start with 3 Wyrd, buy a 2 dot Merit for No Seeming, and then buy a 3 dot Merit for Lethal Mien to replicate the Hunterheart Kith, all at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lethal Mien also stacks with the Hunterheart Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T23:13:19-07:00","id":117440,"title":"","content":"I am well aware that you can. The post I was referring to originally was discussing how merits like Lethal Mien let you replicate Hunterheart despite being a No Seeming Changeling, demonstrating how little you miss out on when using the No Seeming merit. I was pointing out that you end up spending a lot of experience replicating an effect a normal character gets for free. I considered mentioning that the normal character could spend the same experience for an even better effect, but decided the post was getting wordy enough as it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T20:52:55-07:00","id":117824,"title":"","content":"So after reading over the feedback I am getting here, I think I am gonna make No Seeming just a character option without a cost. The lack of a Seeming Curse is nice, but you lose out on any Seeming blessing, kith bonuses, fewer favored contracts, fewer Entitlement options (but not much fewer, like 1 less on average of a zillion you can usually only pick one of) and other such. You can substitute a lot of Kith bonuses...or pay the same to stack them and be that much cooler in those cases. That's a whole list of negatives, but I am aware the Clarity boost and no Curse is nice, hence it is not a flaw or anything you are compensated for, but not something I feel like having people pay for the privilege of.<br /> <br /> Gotten less feedback On the Order...I am leaning toward ignoring it as harsh but I am still quite open to feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">